# Cloudflare Pages redirects & SPA fallback.
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>   (first match wins; keep the SPA fallback LAST)
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# --- Old WordPress URL 301 map (fill in from Google Search Console / old WP sitemap) ---
# Pull the real indexed URLs so nothing that ranks 404s after cutover. Examples:
# /career/            /careers            301
# /category/articles  /roots              301
# /contact-us/        /contact            301

# --- Legacy internal paths ---
/3d        /products/designer   301

# --- Vanity URL: /meet forwards to the HubSpot consultation booking page. ---
/meet      https://meetings-na2.hubspot.com/introduction/janta-power   302

# --- Never let missing hashed build assets fall through to the SPA shell. ---
# Without this, a request that races a deploy (asset not yet live at an edge
# node) gets served index.html as a "200", which /assets/* and /models/*'s
# `immutable, max-age=1y` header then caches forever as if it were the real
# file — poisoning that URL with HTML disguised as JS until manually purged.
# A real 404 here is never cached as a valid response.
/assets/*   /assets/:splat   404
/models/*   /models/:splat   404

# --- SPA fallback: every unmatched path serves the app shell (BrowserRouter) ---
# Keep this as the LAST rule. Without it, deep links like /quiz, /roots 404 on refresh.
/*   /index.html   200
